# BizMate AI Architecture
Version: 1.0
Status: Approved
Last Updated: 2026-07-26

---

# 1. Purpose

This document defines the complete software architecture for BizMate AI.

It serves as the authoritative technical blueprint for developers, AI coding assistants, testers, architects, and future contributors.

Whenever implementation decisions conflict with this document, this Architecture document takes precedence unless superseded by the Master Blueprint.

---

# 2. Architectural Goals

BizMate AI is designed to be:

• Mobile-first

• Offline-first

• AI-first

• Secure by default

• Event-driven

• Modular

• Highly scalable

• Easy to maintain

• Multi-tenant

• Cloud-native

---

# 3. Core Principles

## Simplicity

The user experience must remain extremely simple regardless of the complexity of the underlying architecture.

Business owners should never need technical knowledge to use the application.

---

## Reliability

No financial transaction should ever be silently lost.

Every critical operation must be auditable.

---

## AI Assistance

Artificial Intelligence assists users.

Artificial Intelligence never performs financial actions without explicit user confirmation.

---

## Offline First

Users must be able to continue working without Internet connectivity.

Data synchronisation occurs automatically when connectivity returns.

---

## Security

Every request must be authenticated.

Every database operation must be authorised.

Every financial action must be traceable.

---

## Scalability

The architecture must support future expansion without requiring major redesign.

Examples include:

- Inventory Management
- Purchase Orders
- Payroll
- Accounting
- CRM
- Multi-Branch Operations
- APIs
- Third-party integrations

