# 14. AI Memory

AI Memory stores confirmed business knowledge.

Examples:

Frequently sold products

Customer aliases

Preferred payment methods

Frequently used wording

Recent conversations

Business terminology

AI Memory must never store unconfirmed information.

Memory is retrieved to improve future suggestions.

The AI Memory layer must support Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG).

Model fine-tuning is outside the scope of Version 1.

---

# 15. Offline Synchronisation

Offline capability is a first-class feature.

When offline:

Transactions are stored locally.

A sync queue records:

- Entity
- Operation
- Payload
- Timestamp
- Retry count
- Status

When connectivity returns:

The Sync Service uploads pending changes.

Successful uploads are acknowledged.

Failed uploads remain in the queue until resolved.

Duplicate uploads are prevented through idempotency keys.

